enchilada: battery: real SOC/charging/voltage/current/temperature from PMI8998 over SPMI, read only

SweetBattery reported a static 100 % on the OnePlus 6 (sweetbattery=1 polls sweet's PM6150, wrong
PMIC here). With no boot-arg it now probes PMI8998 on SID 2 (REVID 0x104 = 0x51, 0x105 = 0x15,
REV4 0x103 >= 2; qcom-spmi-pmic.c) and, only on a match, samples the SMB2 charger (0x1006/0x1007
status, 0x1310 USBIN plugin, 0x160b power path; qcom_pmi8998_charger.c) and the FG ADC registers
that need no SRAM handshake (0x41a0 VBATT 122.07 uV, 0x41a2 IBATT 488.281 uA, 0x4150 BATT_TEMP,
0x4009/0x400a MONOTONIC_SOC; RFC pmi8998_fg.c, downstream fg-gen3). The percentage is a smoothed
OCV estimate (VBATT - IBATT x 120 mOhm) on a 4.4 V-class curve, held monotonic per charge
direction; FG MSOC is published only as SweetBatteryFGMonotonicSOC because OnePlus runs fg-gen3
with oem,use_external_fg and Android showed bq27541 31 % vs bms 51 % (PLAN-ENCHILADA.md 12). Design
and max capacity 3300 mAh (mainline enchilada DT, OP_3300mah); temperature published when 0-45 C,
else 25 C. USBIN is read every 2 s, a full sample on a cable change or every 30 s. SPMI glitches
keep the last sample; 10 failed samples fall back to the static source. sweetbattery=0 forces the
static source, sweetbattery=1 keeps the PM6150 path. sweet_spmi_read() only gains READ access to
SID 2 peripherals 0x01, 0x10, 0x13, 0x16, 0x40, 0x41; no write path is added or used.

